send_message, reply_to_message and update_message could only send text, so a bot could not post Adaptive Cards. They now take optional attachments (Teams-supported Bot Framework card content types, enforced by the action schema) and attachmentLayout; text becomes optional with attachments. update_message replaces the whole message so cards can be swapped. Messages above Teams' documented 100 KB bot message limit (UTF-16) are refused before sending; the 28 KB figure in the request is Microsoft's Incoming Webhook limit, not the bot limit.
